WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.118 --> 00:00:01.229
- We're ready to jump.

00:00:01.229 --> 00:00:03.999
One, two, three!

00:00:03.999 --> 00:00:07.096
(energetic music)

00:00:08.456 --> 00:00:11.295
We're here at the MuckFest MS Mud Run.

00:00:11.295 --> 00:00:14.696
It's an event to raise money
for the National MS Society

00:00:14.696 --> 00:00:16.670
and help people fight MS

00:00:16.670 --> 00:00:18.933
and end the disease forever.

00:00:18.933 --> 00:00:20.675
- [Voiceover] I'm ready to win,
I'm going to win this thing.

00:00:20.675 --> 00:00:22.071
- Well, you know, it's a charity mud run.

00:00:22.071 --> 00:00:22.950
You don't need to win.

00:00:22.950 --> 00:00:23.833
- [Voiceover] Okay.

00:00:23.833 --> 00:00:25.370
I'm going to beat Ned at this.

00:00:25.370 --> 00:00:27.646
- That's fine. That's fine.

00:00:27.646 --> 00:00:29.194
We've got a whole crew, my wife is here.

00:00:29.194 --> 00:00:31.203
There's so many people that
have come out to support

00:00:31.203 --> 00:00:34.140
whether it be runners or
volunteers or staff members.

00:00:34.140 --> 00:00:35.242
Hello!

00:00:35.242 --> 00:00:36.578
What does this event mean to you?

00:00:36.578 --> 00:00:39.538
- I have MS, so this is
very meaningful to me.

00:00:39.538 --> 00:00:43.246
- One of my best friends has
MS and I do it for the cause.

00:00:43.246 --> 00:00:44.546
- [Man] We are here with...

00:00:44.546 --> 00:00:45.557
- Teresa Caceres.

00:00:45.557 --> 00:00:46.805
- [ Man] We actually
were running next to them

00:00:46.805 --> 00:00:48.767
for like half of the Mud Run, right.

00:00:48.767 --> 00:00:51.402
- Yes, I was diagnosed with MS in 2007.

00:00:51.402 --> 00:00:53.666
I get numbness and
tingling, I get vertigo,

00:00:53.666 --> 00:00:55.897
I had symptoms for about 7 years

00:00:55.897 --> 00:00:57.617
and had no idea what it was.

00:00:57.617 --> 00:00:59.750
Doctors said I was fine,
nothing's wrong with me

00:00:59.750 --> 00:01:02.177
and I was adamant and I kept
just going back to the doctor

00:01:02.177 --> 00:01:03.930
until finally they gave me an MRI

00:01:03.930 --> 00:01:05.578
and that's what diagnosed me.

00:01:05.578 --> 00:01:06.937
- Because this really
could afflict anybody.

00:01:06.937 --> 00:01:07.738
- It could.

00:01:07.738 --> 00:01:10.389
I lost all mobility in my right arm,

00:01:10.389 --> 00:01:12.130
I couldn't pick up a pen.

00:01:12.130 --> 00:01:14.649
It happened right after I had my son.

00:01:14.649 --> 00:01:18.475
It was pretty horrible.

00:01:19.078 --> 00:01:20.992
- But I just saw you swinging across ropes

00:01:20.992 --> 00:01:24.231
and running through like muddy obstacles.

00:01:24.231 --> 00:01:26.598
You're definitely kicking
MS's butt for sure.

00:01:26.598 --> 00:01:28.420
- I sure am kicking MS's butt.

00:01:28.420 --> 00:01:31.996
So is my daughter and so
is the 25 members who came.

00:01:31.996 --> 00:01:34.874
- And I just love that all of
my friends have come together.

00:01:34.874 --> 00:01:37.196
- Everyone is super enthusiastic,

00:01:37.196 --> 00:01:38.277
I absolutely love the energy,

00:01:38.277 --> 00:01:39.784
everyone is just ready to get all dirty.

00:01:39.784 --> 00:01:41.957
- [Voiceover] It means the
world, you're doing something fun

00:01:41.957 --> 00:01:44.754
just to continue the research of something

00:01:44.754 --> 00:01:46.902
that can help millions of people.

00:01:46.902 --> 00:01:48.592
It's the world to me.

00:01:48.592 --> 00:01:49.888
- What was the most
difficult obstacle for you?

00:01:49.888 --> 00:01:52.070
- The one across the lake,
that was really cool.

00:01:52.070 --> 00:01:54.287
Just walking over, jumping
over barrels, that was fun.

00:01:54.287 --> 00:01:55.994
- [ Voiceover] The one
where we, like, held on.

00:01:55.994 --> 00:01:57.027
It was like a zipline.

00:01:57.027 --> 00:01:58.188
- [ Voiceover] Oh the zipline ring.

00:01:58.188 --> 00:01:59.430
- [Voiceover] I did a front flip

00:01:59.430 --> 00:02:00.730
into the water at that point.

00:02:00.730 --> 00:02:02.588
- [Voiceover] Being tagged
and then being tackled.

00:02:02.588 --> 00:02:04.712
- [Voiceover] The general rope net climb.

00:02:04.712 --> 00:02:05.594
- What was that like?

00:02:05.594 --> 00:02:08.532
- It was easy.

00:02:08.532 --> 00:02:10.389
- I mean the reason I come here is because

00:02:10.389 --> 00:02:12.409
I love laughing, I love seeing
my dad run through the mud

00:02:12.409 --> 00:02:15.253
and just the laughter
everyday gets me through.

00:02:15.253 --> 00:02:18.074
- Do some research, realize
that it affects so many people.

00:02:18.074 --> 00:02:20.025
MS Society has their website,

00:02:20.025 --> 00:02:22.625
you can also look up MuckFest
MS, it's all over the country.

00:02:22.625 --> 00:02:24.865
- We just did a Mud Run, thanks so much

00:02:24.865 --> 00:02:26.769
to the National MS Society.

00:02:26.769 --> 00:02:30.802
For everyone that wants to
fight MS, we are The Try Guys!

00:02:30.802 --> 00:02:34.546
Argh, get muddy!

00:02:34.546 --> 00:02:36.336
Get muddy!

00:02:36.336 --> 00:02:38.466
- I'm just giving you a sexy water bath.

00:02:38.466 --> 00:02:41.580
(energetic, rhythmic rock music)

00:02:41.580 --> 00:02:42.497
- Why wash your butt alone

00:02:42.497 --> 00:02:44.069
when you can wash your butt with friends?

00:02:44.069 --> 00:02:49.069
(laughter)

